{title: 179 - The Wonders of Redeeming Love}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #179 • LA SIERRA • 8.5.9.6}
{lyricist: Roswell F; Cottrell}
{composer: Perry Beach}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 179}
{meta: tune LA SIERRA}
{meta: meter 8.5.9.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]The wonders [Gm]of [C7]redeeming [F]love
[F]Our highest thoughts exceed;
[Dm]The Son [Am]of [Gm]God [Am]comes [Dm]from [Bb]above
[F]For sinful man to bleed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]He gives [Gm]Himself, [C7]His [Dm]life, [F]His all,
[F]A sinless sacrifice.
[Dm]For [C]man [Gm]He [Am]drains [Dm]the cup of [Bb]gall,
[F]For man the victim dies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]And now before [C7]His Father's [F]face
[F]His precious blood He pleads;
[Dm]For [C]those [Gm]who [Am]seek [Dm]the throne of [Bb]grace
[F]His lovee still intercedes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]He knows the [Gm]frailties [C7]of [F]our frame,
[F]For He has borne our grief;
[Dm]Our [C]great [Gm]High [Am]Priest [Dm]once felt the [Bb]same,
[F]And He can send relief.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]His love will [Gm]not [C7]be [Dm]satisfied,
[F]Till He in glory sees
[Dm]The faithful [Gm]ones [Dm]for whom [Bb]He [F]died
[F]From sin forever free.
{end_of_verse}
